{
  "$comment": "One table, three resolvers: C# ProductPathing (Pe.Shared.Tests RuntimeOwnershipTests), TS host-contracts (runtime-ownership.test.ts), PowerShell Resolve-ProductRuntimeRoot (tools/tests/host-state-isolation.ps1, stateRoots only). Frozen by docs/features/homes/MAP.md freeze shapes 1 to 4 and 7. stateRoots: the machine state root, unchanged; sharedRoot there is the firm-home fence. markers: the text of a pe-home.json and the tier it proves, null when it proves none. homes: pure resolution of the home list [user, project, firm] from injected facts. productHome and sharedRoot are the two environment overrides; existing is the set of folders that exist; markerFiles maps a folder to the text of its pe-home.json; pointer is data.path of the model's project-home blob. %DOCUMENTS% is the machine's Documents known folder. The firm home is sharedRoot when it is non-blank, else the literal default folder, and only when that folder exists. No marker is read for it, and a chosen folder that does not exist never falls back to the default. sharedDriveRoot is the firm home's grandparent. The project home is <sharedDriveRoot>\\<pointer>\\Pe.Tools, accepted only when its marker reads project. stateTree: every homes folder sits under the state root's state\\ folder. podlessRuns is where a run with no pod writes. trayLaunches: TS trayOwnerArguments emits argv; C# Pe.Host.Tray Program.ParseOwner must accept it.",
